# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets and host
# artifacts out of the image.

# ⚠️ Never let .env into an image. SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY is the service-role key --
# it bypasses RLS entirely. In ECS it arrives via the task definition's `secrets`
# block from SSM Parameter Store, never baked into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reinstalled in the image; a host node_modules may hold the wrong platform's
# binaries.
node_modules
dist

# Tests and their fixtures do not belong in a runtime image. test/helpers/ can
# delete live database rows.
test
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
coverage

.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
.eslintrc*
eslint.config.*
.prettierrc*
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
